<title>UK: BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of quarter-final first leg matches in the men's EuroLeague basketball championship on Thursday:</p>
<p>In Istanbul:</p>
<p>Efes Pilsen (Turkey) 87 Villeurbanne (France) 71 (halftime 41-32).</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Efes Pilsen - Petar Naumoski 23, Ufuk Sarica 18.</p>
<p>Villeurbanne - Jim Bilba 18, Brian Howard 15.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,000  </p>
<p>In Athens:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos (Greece) 49 Olympiakos (Greece) 69 (29-30)</p>
<p>Leading  scorers:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos - Byron Dinkins 12, Frangiskos Alvertis 12, Feran Martinez 9</p>
<p>Olympiakos - David Rivers 17, Dragan Tarlac 16, Panayotis Fasoulas 8</p>
<p>Attendance - 18,000  </p>
<p>In Bologna:</p>
<p>Team System Bologna (Italy) 70 Barcelona (Spain)  65 (37-33)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Bologna - Eric Murdock 21, Carlton Myers 18, Conrad McRae 9</p>
<p>Barcelona - Arturas Karnishova 18, Alexanda Djordjevic 11, Ramon Rivas 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 7,000  </p>
<p>In Milan:</p>
<p>Stefanel Milan (Italy) 94 Olimpija Ljubljana (Slovenia) 90 (43-40)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Stefanel - Flavio Portaluppi 17, Alessandro De Pol 17, Gregor Fucka 16, Marco Sambugaro 12</p>
<p>Olimpija - Aeriel McDonald 28, Marko Tusek 12,  Darren Henrie 12, Marijan Kraljevic 11</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,500</p>
</text>
